 stem:"A 45-year-old man from a rural area who drinks untreated well water has had progressive darkening of his skin for 2 years. Examination shows diffuse hyperpigmentation with scattered small hypopigmented spots on the trunk ('raindrop' pattern) and multiple hard, wart-like keratotic papules on both palms and soles. He also has decreased pinprick sensation in a stocking–glove distribution. Chronic exposure to which of the following is the most likely cause?",
